==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ɹʊm/|/ɹuːm/}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-room.ogg|Audio (UK with /ʊ/)}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ɹum/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-room.ogg|Audio (US with /u/)}}
* {{a|New England|Tidewater}} {{IPA|en|/ɹʊm/}}
* {{homophone|en|rheum|q={{IPAchar|/ɹum/}}}}
* {{homophone|en|rum|q={{IPAchar|/ɹʊm/}}; without foot–strut split}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːm|ʊm|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|roum}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rūm||room, space}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*rūm||room}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*rūmą||room}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*rewh₁-||free space}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nds|Ruum}}, {{cog|nl|ruimte||space}} and {{cog|nl|ruim||cargo load}}, {{cog|de|Raum||space, interior space}}, {{cog|da|rum||space, locality}}, {{cog|no|rom||space}}, {{cog|sv|rum||space, location}}, and also with {{cog|la|rūs||country, field, farm}} through Indo-European. More at {{l|en|rural}}.

It is ostensibly an exception to the [[w:Great Vowel Shift|Great Vowel Shift]], which otherwise would have produced the pronunciation {{IPAchar|/ɹaʊm/}}, but {{IPAchar|/aʊ/}} does not occur before noncoronal consonants in Modern English native vocabulary.

